From: SP11 Linux Project <272055834+geocausa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH RFC] wifi: ath12k: write scan_priority to WMI cmd and restore country code on resume

STATUS: RFC / SOURCE-VERIFIED ONLY — NOT YET COMPILED OR HARDWARE-TESTED.

On Surface Pro 11 (X1E80100 + WCN7850) running Linux 7.3 without WoWLAN,
every suspend/resume cycle (and cold boot) exhibits a ~15.6 s initial scan
before Wi-Fi authentication begins, followed by < 0.8 s auth/DHCP:

  T =  0.00 s: firmware cold-boots, resets phy0 regdom to WORLD ("00"),
               supplicant initiates 101-channel scan (2.4/5/6 GHz, passive)
  T = +7.02 s: firmware 802.11d offload scan discovers local country ("GB")
  T = +15.58 s: first scan finishes; auth + DHCP complete in 0.77 s

Two driver issues in ath12k contribute directly:

1. drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c (ath12k_wmi_send_scan_start_cmd):
   The driver computes arg->scan_priority (WMI_SCAN_PRIORITY_MEDIUM when
   ar->state_11d == ATH12K_11D_PREPARING, otherwise WMI_SCAN_PRIORITY_LOW)
   so the initial host scan will not be preempted by the MEDIUM-priority
   firmware 11d scan, but never writes arg->scan_priority into
   cmd->scan_priority. Because the WMI skb is zero-allocated, firmware
   always receives WMI_SCAN_PRIORITY_VERY_LOW (0).

2. drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c (ath12k_mac_op_reconfig_complete):
   ath12k already restores cached ar->alpha2 to firmware after crash
   recovery (IEEE80211_RECONFIG_TYPE_RESTART), but returns early for
   suspend/resume (IEEE80211_RECONFIG_TYPE_SUSPEND). Because WCN7850
   cold-boots on resume without WoWLAN and sends default "00" (WORLD),
   every wake drops the previously learned country code, expands the
   channel list from 64 local channels to 101 passive WORLD channels,
   and re-triggers a full 802.11d scan.

Note: On kernels with CONFIG_ATH_REG_DYNAMIC_USER_REG_HINTS unset,
userspace hints (`iw reg set`) are ignored by ath12k_reg_notifier(), so
this must be fixed in the driver (and paired with userspace known-freq
scanning such as iwd if sub-2s reconnect is desired).

Signed-off-by: SP11 Linux Project <272055834+geocausa@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c |  1 +
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
index 2c51d35..f874d99 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -13546,6 +13546,26 @@ ath12k_mac_op_reconfig_complete(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 
 	lockdep_assert_wiphy(hw->wiphy);
 
+	if (reconfig_type == IEEE80211_RECONFIG_TYPE_SUSPEND) {
+		guard(mutex)(&ah->hw_mutex);
+		if (ah->state != ATH12K_HW_STATE_ON)
+			return;
+
+		for_each_ar(ah, ar, i) {
+			if (ar->ab->hw_params->current_cc_support &&
+			    ar->alpha2[0] != 0 && ar->alpha2[1] != 0) {
+				struct wmi_set_current_country_arg arg = {};
+
+				ah->regd_updated = false;
+				memcpy(&arg.alpha2, ar->alpha2, 2);
+				reinit_completion(&ar->regd_update_completed);
+				ath12k_wmi_send_set_current_country_cmd(ar, &arg);
+				ath12k_mac_11d_scan_stop(ar);
+			}
+		}
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (reconfig_type != IEEE80211_RECONFIG_TYPE_RESTART)
 		return;
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
index d5160af..0028b88 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -2704,6 +2704,7 @@ int ath12k_wmi_send_scan_start_cmd(struct ath12k *ar,
 		arg->scan_priority = WMI_SCAN_PRIORITY_MEDIUM;
 	else
 		arg->scan_priority = WMI_SCAN_PRIORITY_LOW;
+	cmd->scan_priority = cpu_to_le32(arg->scan_priority);
 	cmd->notify_scan_events = cpu_to_le32(arg->notify_scan_events);
 
 	ath12k_wmi_copy_scan_event_cntrl_flags(cmd, arg);
